#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-diff-pairs(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:7
msgid "git-diff-pairs - Compare the content and mode of provided blob pairs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:12
msgid "git diff-pairs -z [<diff-options>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:19
msgid ""
"Show changes for file pairs provided on stdin. Input for this command must "
"be in the NUL-terminated raw output format as generated by commands such as "
"`git diff-tree -z -r --raw`. By default, the outputted diffs are computed "
"and shown in the patch format when stdin closes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:23
msgid ""
"A single NUL byte may be written to stdin between raw input lines to compute "
"file pair diffs up to that point instead of waiting for stdin to close. A "
"NUL byte is also written to the output to delimit between these batches of "
"diffs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:28
msgid ""
"Usage of this command enables the traditional diff pipeline to be broken up "
"into separate stages where `diff-pairs` acts as the output phase. Other "
"commands, such as `diff-tree`, may serve as a frontend to compute the raw "
"diff format used as input."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:33
msgid ""
"Instead of computing diffs via `git diff-tree -p -M` in one step, `diff-"
"tree` can compute the file pairs and rename information without the blob "
"diffs. This output can be fed to `diff-pairs` to generate the underlying "
"blob diffs as done in the following example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:37
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git diff-tree -z -r -M $a $b |\n"
"git diff-pairs -z\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:42
msgid ""
"Computing the tree diff upfront with rename information allows patch output "
"from `diff-pairs` to be progressively computed over the course of "
"potentially multiple invocations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:45
msgid ""
"Pathspecs are not currently supported by `diff-pairs`. Pathspec limiting "
"should be performed by the upstream command generating the raw diffs used as "
"input."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:47
msgid "Tree objects are not currently supported as input and are rejected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-diff-pairs.adoc:50
msgid ""
"Abbreviated object IDs in the `diff-pairs` input are not supported. "
"Outputted object IDs can be abbreviated using the `--abbrev` option."
msgstr ""

